# React JSX safety (DinnerDeck)

## Valid tags only

- Use standard HTML elements in JSX: `div`, `span`, `button`, `p`, `h1`–`h6`, etc.
- **Never** invent tags like `motion.div`, `motion.span`, or mismatched open/close pairs (`<motion.div>` … `</div>`).

## Where UI lives

- Bottom sheets / pickers: edit `src/components/MealPickerSheet.tsx`, `KidsPickerSheet.tsx`, or `sheets.module.css` — not large inline blocks in `page.tsx`.
- After any JSX edit in `src/**/*.tsx`, run `npm run check` before finishing.

## Sheet pattern

```tsx
<div className={styles.overlay} onClick={onClose}>
  <div className={styles.sheet} onClick={e => e.stopPropagation()}>
    ...
  </div>
</div>
```

## Nested controls

- Do not put `<button>` inside `<button>`.
- Info/actions inside a row: use a `div` row with `onClick`, and a separate `<button type="button">` with `stopPropagation` for secondary actions.
